        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#155eef]">The simple way to optimize images</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.05em] text-[#111318] sm:text-4xl">A free image size reducer built for real-world file limits.</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-[15px] leading-7 text-[#69707d]">
          <p>Large image files are frustrating when you need to send an email, upload a profile photo, meet a website limit, or share a picture quickly. Image Size Reducer gives you a direct answer: choose your target, add an image, and get a smaller file in seconds. Instead of guessing with a quality slider, you can reduce image size to under 100 KB, 500 KB, 1 MB, 2 MB, or any custom limit. The result is made for the exact constraint you are trying to meet.</p>
          <p>This image size reducer works with the formats people use every day, including JPG, JPEG, PNG, and WebP. You can also use it as an image size converter when you need a JPG, PNG, or WebP output. Converting format can make a meaningful difference for photographs, product images, screenshots, and graphics. The output format, target size, quality floor, and maximum width are all available in one focused workspace, so you can change image size without opening several different tools.</p>
          <p>Image quality matters as much as file size. Our automatic compression process searches for the best quality that stays under your chosen target whenever the image can achieve it. If a very small target requires more than compression alone, the tool gently reduces the dimensions while preserving the original aspect ratio. This gives you the best practical balance between a smaller file and image quality that still looks good on screens. You can also set a maximum width when you want an easy resize for a website, marketplace, social profile, or email attachment.</p>
          <p>Need to process more than one file? Add up to 20 images at once and apply the same settings to the whole batch. Each result includes the original size, reduced size, savings percentage, and output dimensions, making it easy to compare the results before downloading. Download one image individually or download the complete batch as a ZIP file. Batch processing stays free, with no account, watermark, subscription, or daily limit getting in the way.</p>
          <p>Privacy is built into the way Image Size Reducer works. Your images are processed locally in your browser using standard web capabilities, so they do not need to be sent to a server or stored in an account. That makes this a useful free image reducer for personal photos, private documents, work files, and client assets. When you close the page, your original files remain on your device and the tool has nothing waiting for you online.</p>
          <p>Whether you call it an image size reducer, an image size converter, or an easy resize tool, the goal is the same: make an image fit where you need it without unnecessary steps. Upload a file, select the limit or format you need, and download the finished image. Image Size Reducer is designed to keep that workflow fast, clear, and free while helping you preserve the image quality that matters.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-[780px] border-t border-[#dfe2e7] pt-12 sm:mt-28 sm:pt-16" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
