        <div class="mt-8 divide-y divide-[#dfe2e7] border-y border-[#dfe2e7]">
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>Will resizing reduce image quality?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Resizing reduces the number of pixels, so some fine detail can be lost when making an image smaller. Image Size Reducer keeps the original aspect ratio and uses the largest practical dimensions and quality for your target, helping images stay crisp.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>How do I reduce image size to 50KB online for free?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Upload your image, enter 50 in the Custom target field, select KB, and choose Reduce images. The tool adjusts quality and dimensions when necessary to get as close to 50KB as possible while staying under your target.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>What image formats can I compress?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">You can upload JPG, JPEG, PNG, and WebP images. Choose JPG, PNG, or WebP as the output format before processing.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>Does compressing an image reduce quality?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Lossy compression can reduce some visual detail, especially at very small file sizes. The compressor searches for the highest quality that meets your target and lets you set a quality floor for more control.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>What is the difference between resizing, compressing, and cropping?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Resizing changes pixel dimensions, compressing reduces file size in KB or MB, and cropping removes part of the image. This tool supports resizing and compression without changing your image framing.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>How do I compress an image online?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Drop an image or choose one from your device, select a target or output setting, and click Reduce images. Preview the result and download it immediately without installing software.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>How do I resize an image to a specific KB size?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Enter the required number in the Custom target field, or choose 100 KB, 500 KB, 1 MB, or 2 MB. The tool combines compression with dimension reduction if needed.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>What is lossless image compression?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Lossless compression reduces file size without changing pixel data. It is best for graphics where every pixel must remain identical, while JPG or WebP may achieve smaller files for photographs.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>Is this image size reducer free?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Yes. Image Size Reducer is free to use with batch processing, no account, no subscription, no watermark, and no daily credit limit.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>How do I change image dimensions in pixels?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Choose a maximum width such as 2400, 1920, 1200, or 800 pixels. Height is calculated from the original aspect ratio so the image is not stretched.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>Is the image compressor free and private?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Yes. Processing happens locally in your browser, so images are not uploaded to or stored on a server by this tool.</p></details>
          <details class="group py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[#111318] sm:text-lg"><span>How do I resize an image without losing quality?</span><span class="text-xl font-normal text-[#a4a9b3] transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-[680px] text-sm leading-6 text-[#69707d]">Use the largest maximum width that meets your needs, keep the quality floor high, and avoid unnecessary resizing. Preserving the aspect ratio also prevents distortion.</p></details>
        </div>
